id: pm-memory-sdk-secret-scan
title: Delegate memory credential detection to SDK mutation secret scanner
description: "Implements companion pm-cli-website-d8bz G7. Delegate shared credential grammars to scanMutationSecrets, preserving explicit email consent and narrowly documented stronger memory rules."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: "gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1704","gh:unbraind/pm-memory#51","gh:unbraind/pm-memory#58",sdk-adoption
created_at: "2026-11-06T10:08:57.274Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-11T13:57:36.281Z"
author: codex-sol
parent: pm-memory-0kwy
comments[72]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T10:09:03.989Z",codex-sol,"Companion pm-cli-website-d8bz is read-only specification. Compare every existing credential rule against the public scanner before removal; retain local email, retention and identity/path policies, with real no-git tracker refusal and allowance tests."
  "2026-11-06T10:20:27.959Z",codex-sol,"Shared provider credential rules now use scanMutationSecrets. Supplements cover low-entropy and alias assignments, 16-character legacy keys, authorization headers, URL passwords, unbounded JWTs and mixed-case/long private-key markers. Four bounded decoding passes cover encoded/normalized credentials. SDK private-host matching is quadratic on hyphenated noncredentials, so shared scans use overlapping bounded windows with repeated-window reuse; domain path/identity rules retain their scope. See docs/sdk-adoption.md."
  "2026-11-06T10:32:23.053Z",codex-sol,"Validation: shared SDK scanner/decoding behavioral revert failed all 9 provider/encoded cases; the stronger-supplement corpus separately fails on revert because SDK-only provider credentials would enter memory. Restoration passed 15/15 adoption tests and the supplemental case. Linked scanner tests passed 9/9 with pm test --run --progress; adversarial privacy deadline controls passed 4/4. Production dependency audit found zero vulnerabilities. README, architecture and docs/sdk-adoption.md document the SDK floor, preserved local policies and scanner bounds. Full unchanged coverage/release gates remain CI work."
  "2026-11-06T10:37:20.013Z",codex-sol,"Post-PR adversarial inspection found a concrete encoded-credential bypass: a malformed UTF-8 suffix caused decodeURIComponent to retain the entire percent run, concealing an otherwise valid credential prefix. Replace invalid bytes in the inspection view instead, preserving valid decoded bytes. Add a real-tracker non-echoing regression and isolated before/fixed proof before the next review push."
  "2026-11-06T10:45:08.265Z",codex-sol,"Follow-up verification: malformed-percent UTF-8 regression fails against the prior decoder (1 failure) and passes after replacement decoding. Reverting only the scan-window boundary prefix also fails the safe embedded-identifier control (1 failure). Both proofs ran in the disposable worktree; restoration passed all 16 current adoption tests. Focused malformed/boundary controls passed 3/3, adversarial deadlines 4/4, and linked scanner runs passed 10/10 plus the supplemental corpus. Typecheck, lint, duplication and docstrings pass. This follow-up accompanies the code before the next review push."
  "2026-11-06T11:05:08.823Z",codex-sol,"Legacy policy comparison found SDK semantic differences for generic sk prefixes: short Anthropic-style keys fall between provider-specific floors, and the host word-end boundary differs from the older prefix refusal. Preserve the generic legacy prefix supplement after shared scanning, document the reason, and prove the missing cases on a real temporary tracker before batching with review findings."
  "2026-11-06T11:53:32.785Z",codex-sol,"Review round 1: fixed PR 51 thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc60erz8. Long quoted SSH/password values now receive complete quote-span SDK inspection with bounded bodies, normalized prefix whitespace, both quote styles and mixed delimiters; the existing identity exclusions remain unchanged. No SSH/password credential grammar was copied. Reverting sharedCredential alone fails the real-tracker quoted regression (1 failure). Separate legacy-prefix and JWT-union reverts each fail the real-tracker compatibility case (1 each). Restored adoption tests passed 18/18; the linked pm runner also passed all 18 current tests. Adversarial deadline controls passed 4/4 after a necessary at-sign precheck preserved email semantics and avoided needless email backtracking. Lint, typecheck, duplication (0%), docstrings and build pass. The attached exec alert is RegExp.exec, with no process execution API imported."
  "2026-11-06T12:06:24.846Z",codex-sol,"Final wrapper check found that JSON serialization doubles the backslashes in an already escaped credential, leaving separator backslashes in the inspection view. Normalize repeated escape introducers without adding provider grammars; add a real-tracker JSON-wrapped escape regression and a disposable before/fixed proof before the queued second review."
  "2026-11-06T12:21:45.923Z",codex-sol,"Serialized escape wrappers verified: restoring the prior credentialViews decoder fails the JSON-wrapped real-tracker regression (1 failure). Requiring an escape suffix instead of consuming every backslash run fails the independent process deadline regression (1 failure); both restored controls pass. Repeated-backslash normalization remains linear and preserves ordinary backslashes. The final linked adoption run passed 19/19 tests, and the linked adversarial/JWT controls passed 5/5. Lint, typecheck, duplication (0%) and docstrings pass. The second bot review is still queued and will receive this corrected head."
  "2026-11-06T13:00:18.290Z",codex-sol,Review round 2 requests a distinct quoted-span adversarial deadline case. Measure the real SDK path first; retain full quoted credential detection and optimize only if the fixed deadline exposes repeated scan cost. Companion pm-cli-website-d8bz remains read only.
  "2026-11-06T13:13:04.299Z",codex-sol,"Review round 2 fixed: quote-prefix contexts restart at delimiters, and short contiguous spans already covered by raw windows skip redundant SDK calls. Long spans and normalized whitespace still receive complete shared inspection. Added 25000 distinct quoted spans to the unchanged 500ms/process deadline controls; expanded the real-tracker quoted corpus with short credentials behind long whitespace. Final linked adoption run passes 19/19, expanded quoted test 1/1, and linked deadline/JWT run 6/6. Earlier wall-time failures under CPU contention included unchanged controls; the final run passes without threshold changes. Reverting only quotedCredentialViews in a disposable worktree fails the new process-deadline test; restored implementation passes the six-case controls. Lint, typecheck, duplication 0 percent and docstring gates pass. Companion pm-cli-website-d8bz remains read only. Push this fix for review round 3 and final-head full CI."
  "2026-11-06T16:50:30.992Z",codex-sol,"Issue 52 is now included explicitly in this PR and tracked by pm-memory-quoted-credential-keys with its required issue tag. SDK provider rules remain delegated. A narrow quoted-scalar supplement decodes JSON values and bounded serialized copies, preserving reference controls. Export now checks visible content before origin setup and exact output bytes before publication, preserving existing email behavior. Focused five-case regression and seven-case coverage probe pass; every new helper branch is exercised. Full intended-source coverage remains a CI claim."
  "2026-11-06T17:26:58.929Z",codex-sol,"The issue-52 supplement and export boundary are validated: linked security cases 6/6, baseline-array control 1/1, subsequent deadline/JWT controls 6/6, no skips. The mixed broad run had 61/62 passes with only the distinct-quote wall-time control failing before the quieter isolated retry; thresholds were never changed. Known encoded original documents are scanned because they are serialized into portable output. Unshared retention state is preserved. Provider rules still use scanMutationSecrets; generic quoted scalar and bounded decoding policy remain local and documented. Final CI must certify the complete intended source scope."
  "2026-11-06T17:40:18.366Z",codex-sol,"Review round 4 on the preceding head reports adjacent literal suffix masking, long whitespace projection, and missing long distinct-quote deadline controls. Checking each against current source before making changes; the documentation will describe verified final behavior. Issue 52 is pushed in commit 725d9bd."
  "2026-11-06T17:46:16.859Z",codex-sol,"Both round-4 functional regressions pass on genuine temporary SDK trackers: adjacent literal context and unquoted passphrase whitespace, with safe references and retained quoted SSH behavior. The quoted SSH documentation claim itself is confirmed by space, tab and newline controls; that part of the requested documentation downgrade is incorrect. The environment-masking description is corrected to match the new context-preserving behavior."
  "2026-11-06T17:50:56.882Z",codex-sol,"Round-4 evidence: restoring the old privacy masking fails the adjacent-literal regression; disabling the whitespace projection fails the unquoted-assignment regression. Restoring fixed functions passes 2/2. Linked new regressions pass 2/2, existing shared quoted SDK control 1/1, and issue-52 regressions still pass 6/6. Added 2,500 distinct quoted spans over 64 characters under the unchanged deadlines. Eight-character body projections retain the pinned SDK six/eight-character quoted floors; raw windows retain provider tokens. The loaded-host deadline run is 4/7, with escape-run and both distinct-quote timing failures; no thresholds are changed and CI must certify performance. Typecheck, lint, duplication 0 percent and docstrings pass. Quoted SSH prefixes already reject long space/tab/newline inputs; retaining that verified documentation claim rather than adding a false limitation."
  "2026-11-06T18:56:26.888Z",codex-sol,"Final-head Node 26 npm and Bun each pass all 720 tests, including all deadline controls, but miss two coverage branches. Core secret admission is 100 across all dimensions. Export has an unnecessary nullish description fallback even though Memory.description is required and the SDK always provides a string. Removing that unreachable fallback; the other missing branch belongs to G1 ownership-field validation."
  "2026-11-06T18:59:56.967Z",codex-sol,"Latest isolated linked deadline/JWT run on the unchanged admission source passes all 7/7 with zero skips, including long distinct quotes, at unchanged scan and process thresholds. Both completed prior CI legs pass 720/720 and core.ts is 100/100/100/100. The export description fallback was unreachable because Memory.description and the public SDK read model require a string; it is removed without changing policy. The focused ownership/baseline/legacy-export probe passes 3/3. Fresh final-head CI must certify the complete gate after this coverage repair."
  "2026-11-06T21:08:03.760Z",codex-sol,"Round 5 confirms a nested-object credential gap. Fixing inherited credential-key context and adding genuine-SDK refusal/reference controls. The public SecretGuardFinding.rule type exposes a literal inventory: use an exhaustive policy map checked against that public union, with unknown runtime findings conservatively refused, rather than freezing the peer range or importing private rules. Keep the explicit user-required 500ms deadline; both Node 26 full gates pass every deadline and 100/100/100/100 coverage."
  "2026-11-06T21:18:17.515Z",codex-sol,"Round-5 linked secret controls pass 2/2. Reverting inherited parent context fails the nested-object case; changing the known identity exclusion fails its accepted control. Omitting npm_token from the exhaustive policy fails typecheck against the public SecretGuardFinding.rule union. Restoring source passes 5/5 joint cases and typecheck. No SDK mocks/private inventory imports are used. The fixed 500ms and process deadlines remain unchanged as required; both completed prior full Node 26 gates pass all deadline cases, 720/720 tests and 100/100/100/100 coverage. The fifth review round is complete; valid findings are fixed and refusals will be answered after the push."
  "2026-11-06T21:27:24.214Z",codex-sol,"The round-5 follow-up correctly notes that exhaustive build-time rule typing cannot constrain a newer runtime SDK under an open peer range. Restricting the supported peer to the reviewed 2026.11.5 inventory, with matching package metadata/docs and an explicit boundary control. Future SDK updates still use the shared scanner; expanding support requires the public rule-union check and genuine SDK compatibility fixtures to pass before changing the peer contract."
  "2026-11-06T21:32:11.373Z",codex-sol,"The final linked round-5 policy suite passes 2/2 with zero skips under the exact 2026.11.5 peer contract. Restoring only the open peer range fails the supported-inventory boundary assertion; restoring the exact peer passes 1/1 with genuine SDK identity/credential checks. Package/lock metadata, README, architecture and SDK adoption docs agree. Typecheck, lint, duplication 0 percent and docstrings pass. This completes the fifth-round compatibility follow-up; future SDK versions require an explicit inventory review before peer support expands."
  "2026-11-06T21:41:06.348Z",codex-sol,"A final public-scanner parity probe found an SDK-positive long private-key marker missed by the bounded adapter when its long prefix has no separating space. Correcting only the documented long-marker supplement to retain the SDK rule across windows, with a genuine-SDK positive fixture and a function-only revert proof. No provider grammar catalogue or other policy changes are added."
  "2026-11-06T21:43:02.868Z",codex-sol,"The long-marker parity control passes 1/1 through the linked runner on a genuine temporary tracker. The public SDK independently reports private_key for the fixture. Reverting only supplementalCredential to the prior function admits the marker and fails the refusal assertion; restoration passes 1/1. The complete marker supplement now preserves the SDK character-class rule across scan windows, including a prefix without a separating space, and retains the stronger case-insensitive policy. Typecheck, lint, duplication 0 percent and docstrings pass. SDK support remains exactly 2026.11.5."
  "2026-11-09T09:35:53.791Z",codex-agent,"Review round 6: merged current main, fetched all four unresolved threads with complete comments, and inspected the latest CodeRabbit review body (no Outside diff range findings). Plan: preserve duplicate credential assignments, inspect overlapping escaped JSON strings, add safe record and field export diagnostics, and strengthen SDK-readable ownership fixtures. Full npm/Bun release gates are deferred to CI under the review task host-duration exception. Baseline health reports extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew (pinned host 2026.11.5, discovered pm-github 2026.11.8); dependency pins remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-09T09:39:35.551Z",codex-agent,"Implemented duplicate-preserving JSON member inspection (including numeric, escaped-name, prototype-name and nested object/array duplicates) and overlapping unescaped quote boundaries. Genuine no-git tracker tests exercise remember/import, readable legacy data, pre-publication refusal, safe short values and environment/secret-manager references. Export refusals now name the native record id and field without copying content. Unchanged adversarial and JWT controls pass 7/7. Clean-HOME strict health passes all 10 checks; the normal host-only extension skew is absent in that CI-like environment."
  "2026-11-09T09:42:40.185Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs in a disposable worktree: restoring only duplicate JSON parsing/member traversal makes the duplicate credential members test fail (1 failure); restoring only nonoverlapping quote cursor advancement makes stray prose quotes fail (1 failure); restoring only the pre-context export privacy loop makes the native-field and decoded-original diagnostic tests fail (2 failures). Fixed restoration passes 1/1, 1/1 and 2/2 respectively. Same-class self-review added duplicate numeric/escaped/prototype keys, nested values and duplicate descendants, serialized wrappers, import/export boundary controls, plus safe reference/short-value controls."
  "2026-11-09T09:43:57.179Z",codex-agent,"Broader regression command passed 41/41 with no skips: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/transfer.test.ts test/review-r1.test.ts test/review-r6.test.ts test/review-r7.test.ts test/edges.test.ts. Linked security corpus passed 14/14. Typecheck, lint, build, docstrings (173 declarations), duplication (0 percent) and publish-attestation verification pass. Optional production audit could not reach the public advisory endpoint on two attempts; no dependency change is made. The latest review scope notice is unsupported by this task: G1 and G7 are both explicitly authorized and their active feature items are already linked from the PR."
  "2026-11-09T09:44:24.897Z",codex-agent,"Thread mapping: PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc60wKts fixes duplicate assignment loss; PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc60wKtu fixes stray-quote boundary loss; PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc60wKty adds safe record/field export refusals. Revert proofs and exact commands are recorded above. All four unresolved findings are valid and fixed; no outside-diff-range section exists in the latest review body. Full npm/Bun release gates are intentionally left to final-head CI under the explicit long-running-package exception. Both feature items remain in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-09T10:36:27.013Z",pi-agent,"Review round 7 finding (src/transfer.ts export diagnostic): the bare catch collapses every privacy refusal to 'Credential-shaped memory refused'/'Remove credentials' and converts non-MemoryError defects into a credential refusal. Class rule: a mid-pipeline wrapper around the package's own privacy refusals must preserve the real message and remedy with its added record/field context, and rethrow anything that is not a privacy MemoryError. Both wrap sites live in transfer.ts (export field loop, import sourcePrivacy line scan); fixing both through one shared core.ts helper. Adversarial tests: export refuses stored bodies for each distinct refusal mode (credential-shaped, normalization limit, escaped declaration) asserting the real cause+remedy+record/field context, plus a wrapper property control that rethrows arbitrary non-domain values unchanged."
  "2026-11-09T11:08:41.909Z",pi-agent,"Round-7 fix (thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc61NEfw), class rule: a wrapper around the package's own privacy refusals must preserve the real refusal category, message and remedy (adding only its safe context) and rethrow any failure that is not a privacy MemoryError, so defects never masquerade as credential policy. Fixed instances of the class: the export field loop in transfer.ts replaced every thrown value with 'Credential-shaped memory refused'/'Remove credentials' (wrong for the normalization-limit, escaped-declaration and any future privacy cause, and it hid non-MemoryError defects); the import source scan in transfer.ts cast every caught line value to MemoryError without checking. Both now use one shared core.ts helper (privacyRefusal). The class search covered every privacy() call site (commands, SDK paths, import and export, packed npm/bun consumers share the same in-process code): these were the only two wrappers that re-diagnosed a caught value; all other call sites either propagate the refusal or already assert the domain before casting. New adversarial tests: export refusals preserve each real privacy cause and remedy for the exact record and field (credential-shaped, normalization limit, escaped declaration); a wrapper property control that a privacy refusal passes through unchanged and that ordinary errors, TypeError, strings, numbers, null, AggregateError and non-privacy MemoryErrors all rethrow as themselves. docs/sdk-adoption.md documents the preserved-cause contract."
  "2026-11-09T11:08:46.934Z",pi-agent,"Revert proof in a disposable copy of the package worktree: reverting only the export field-loop wrapper back to the bare catch with the fixed 'Credential-shaped memory refused' message fails the new cause-preservation control (1 failure: the normalization-limit and escaped-declaration fixtures report the wrong cause and remedy); the wrapper property control is unaffected because it exercises the shared helper. Restoring the wrapper passes both controls."
  "2026-11-09T11:36:14.749Z",pi-agent,"Round-7 final gates at the pushed head: all 12 linked tests pass through pm test --run --progress (including the three new export-cause controls); the focused suites pass 26/26 (transfer + quoted credentials) and 3/3 (export credential original); typecheck, lint, docstring, duplication (0%) and identity (0 violations) pass; the changelog was regenerated after the tracker writes. An earlier pm test run recorded 2 assertion failures in the adversarial wall-time deadline controls (fixed time bound cases) under concurrent host load; the identical rerun passes 12/12, matching the known flaky-under-load behavior documented on 2026-11-06. CI certifies the complete gate."
  "2026-11-09T13:22:58.125Z",codex-agent,"Continuation: confirmed PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc61RCfH on the existing PR branch, with current origin/main already an ancestor and a clean worktree. Rule: reference exemptions must preserve adjacent literal credential context; explanatory suffix recognition must inspect a bounded span. Search found one reference mask in src/core.ts, shared by memory writes, utility and guidance evidence, imports and exports. Will cover credential aliases, reference forms, quoted/encoded inputs, real non-git trackers, CLI JSON/TOON and packed npm/Bun consumers. The latest CodeRabbit scope warning is factually incorrect: the original task explicitly authorizes combined G1 transaction-reader and G7 scanner adoption, recorded in both active feature items and the existing PR body. No Outside diff range findings or additional unresolved threads were returned."
  "2026-11-09T13:28:18.823Z",codex-agent,"The cross-grammar refusal corpus exposed two adjacent instances: passphrase was missing from the unquoted generic-assignment supplement, and scanner-only fallback could miss whitespace-bearing suffixes after a short first token. Added the alias at the unchanged eight-character floor. Unrecognized parenthesized suffixes now refuse directly; recognized multiword prose is bounded to 200 characters and its closing boundary is checked against the complete input. Added a 2160-case alias/reference/quote/separator/encoding corpus, exact-boundary controls, all SDK memory/evidence fields, both harness intake/export paths, legacy read compatibility and a single integrity-checked packed artifact exercised through npm and Bun in non-git consumers. Existing tests and thresholds are unchanged; a new repeated-reference deadline case uses the existing process and scan limits."
  "2026-11-09T13:29:56.246Z",codex-agent,"Packed CLI verification exposed the same privacy boundary in diagnostics: the package returned a safe refusal but the pinned host reconstructed a recovery bundle containing the refused operand. Inspected public CreatePmCliExpectedErrorOptions and PmCliErrorRecoveryPayload; recovery.attempted_command and recovery.normalized_args are supported overrides, so this is not an SDK gap. Every memory privacy refusal now supplies redacted recovery data, covering every command and both JSON/text outputs. The packed regression checks the complete diagnostic and preserves the existing privacy exit code 4. Initial broad run: 59/61 passed; the new packed fixture initially expected the wrong exit code and exposed the recovery echo, and the unchanged long-quote timing control exceeded its scan limit under contention. Isolated timing retry passes all 7/7 at unchanged thresholds, including the new repeated-reference case. Final fixed packed and command tests are running."
  "2026-11-09T13:35:56.268Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs completed in a disposable worktree with the fixed source restored in finally after each mutation. Command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/reference-suffix.test.ts. Fixed baseline: 4/4 pass. Reverting only privacy to the parent implementation: 4 failures. Reverting only supplementalCredential: the grammar corpus fails on punctuation-prefixed unquoted passphrase literals (1 failure, 3 passes). Reverting only runCommand: the recovery-metadata regression fails (1 failure, 3 passes). Every restoration reran and passed all 4/4 tests. The primary PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc61RCfH regression covers 2160 alias/reference/quote/separator/encoding combinations plus 200-character closing-boundary and safe-reference controls. No existing tests or thresholds were weakened."
  "2026-11-09T13:38:46.806Z",codex-agent,"Final continuation validation: the latest linked regression command (pm test pm-memory-sdk-secret-scan --run --only-last --progress) passes 67/67 tests with zero skips, including the 2160-case grammar corpus, genuine non-git SDK/evidence/intake/export controls, all command tests and one integrity-verified archive installed through both npm and Bun with JSON/text CLI refusals. The prior narrower linked command also passed 10/10. Typecheck, lint, build, duplication (0 percent), docstrings (174 declarations), release-publish attestation, production audit (zero vulnerabilities) and strict health (all 10 checks, two pre-existing advisory warnings) pass. An earlier loaded-host long-quote timing failure passed all 7/7 unchanged deadline controls on isolated retry. Full npm and Bun release/coverage gates remain delegated to final-head CI under the explicit pm-memory runtime exception; no thresholds changed. CI branch runs: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/actions?query=branch%3Aadopt-sdk-transaction-readers-and-secret-scan . The claim will be released; this item remains in progress for orchestrator verification. No review thread replies, resolutions, merges or releases were performed."
  "2026-11-09T17:28:27.275Z",codex-agent,"Continuation: preserved the remote branch and merged origin/main. Reviewing PR 51 unresolved threads PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc61Sg11 and PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc61UGba. General rules: malformed quoted tokens must not trigger repeated suffix scans; network/Bun consumer acceptance belongs outside the default unit/coverage suite. Audit all shared privacy paths, add adversarial deadline and discovery regression tests, retain packed npm/Bun non-git acceptance, and record behavioral revert proofs."
  "2026-11-09T17:39:25.451Z",codex-agent,"Revert proofs completed in a disposable worktree with finally restoration: reverting only quotedAssignmentCredential to the pre-fix implementation makes the unterminated-string deadline regression fail (1 failure of 2 controls); restoration passes 2/2. Renaming the packed consumer back into default discovery fails the discovery contract (1 failure); removing its test:install entry separately fails that contract (1 failure). Each restoration passes, and the final boundary suite passes 5/5. Exact controls: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=unterminated test/review-r1.test.ts; node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"default test and coverage\" test/review-boundaries.test.ts. The focused pm-linked privacy/SDK/CLI suite passes 51/51 with zero skips, including all 9 unchanged scanner deadlines, the 2160-case grammar corpus, non-git tracker boundaries and JSON/TOON output."
  "2026-11-09T17:50:11.803Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance passes 3/3, zero skips, through PM_MEMORY_WORKER_POOL=2 npm run test:install. The suffix scenario verifies one captured archive integrity and installs those exact bytes through npm and Bun, exercising SDK admission/readback, CLI JSON and TOON refusals, both harnesses, a non-git tracker, and the reported large malformed quoted input. The existing packed npm/Bun host acceptance remains required alongside the renamed suffix acceptance. Ordinary unit and coverage discovery no longer requires Bun or network installation. Full release/coverage certification remains pending final-head CI under the explicit long-running-package exception."
  "2026-11-09T17:51:27.859Z",codex-agent,"Final continuation receipt: merged origin/main in 921238c, preserved the existing PR and G1/G7 work, fixed both unresolved threads plus the additional typed-cause review-body finding, and recorded the scope-warning refusal. Local pm-linked gates pass 51/51 privacy/CLI, 117/117 transaction/recovery, 7/7 final cause/boundary, 7/7 writer-lock and 3/3 packed npm/Bun acceptance (zero skips in every gate). All 27 negative controls fail when their individual fix is removed and pass after restoration. Public PR conversation will map each thread to the fix commit and request fresh review without replying to or resolving inline threads. No PM CLI/SDK defect was encountered. Full unchanged release/coverage gates remain for CI; existing health advisories are unchanged."
  "2026-11-09T21:43:18.303Z",pi-agent,"Round-13 fix (thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc61bqZi): the cause-audit rule had two gaps. (1) A MemoryError category that is not a literal (a variable category) skipped the audit entirely; only the three established re-diagnosis categories (privacy, format, schema) are exempt now, and everything else is audited for cause retention. (2) The audit only checked cause retention; it now also requires every direct typed catch translation to rethrow an existing typed error instead of re-coding it, recognizing the conditional-expression guard and the negated foreign-type guard, and exempting the deliberate merge refusal helper (cause always retained) and the bare-catch case (already reported as unretainable). The rule is refactored into a reusable linter helper with a synthetic must-refuse corpus (variable category without cause, variable category without guard, literal category without guard, bare catch, refusal without cause) and a must-allow corpus (guarded literal and variable categories, conditional and negated guards, deliberate refusal re-diagnosis, the three exclusions). Reconciled a stale control from the reference-suffix rounds: a single-word parenthesized reference suffix is deliberately refused by the shipped suffix policy (proven by the packed consumer acceptance gate), so the older free-text probe in the edges control now asserts the multi-word prose form is accepted and the arbitrary single-word suffix refuses. No test was weakened; the stale allowance became a new refusal assertion."
  "2026-11-09T22:07:14.606Z",codex-agent,"Continuation class audit found follow-up false negatives in the newly added invariant: an unrelated negated type check or a rethrow after the translation can satisfy the guard audit even though typed errors are still wrapped. Tighten those proof rules, retain all existing exclusions and controls, expand discovery to scripts and entry points, and add per-site mutation controls. Add direct real-history creator identity preservation coverage on the companion feature item."
  "2026-11-09T22:10:48.443Z",codex-agent,"Independent audit revert proofs in a disposable worktree: restoring the variable-category early skip, skipping bare catches, accepting a late rethrow, or accepting an arbitrary foreign constructor each fails its adversarial control (one assertion failure per mutation); every restoration passes. Commands: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"the cause audit reports\" test/review-boundaries.test.ts and node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"the cause audit rejects misleading\" test/review-boundaries.test.ts. Combined with creator identity, all five behavioral reverts fail as required. Package-wide source discovery covers src, scripts and both entry points; privacy/format/schema syntax protections remain intact. The original bare-catch complaint was already handled; its regression remains required. No outside-diff-range section exists in the latest CodeRabbit review. The scope warning is factually wrong: G1 and G7 are both explicit original task objectives, already documented on the existing PR and feature items."
  "2026-11-09T22:20:32.316Z",codex-agent,"Final continuation gates: linked focused origin/boundary command passes 20/20, and linked PM_MEMORY_WORKER_POOL=2 npm run test:install passes all 3/3 packed npm/Bun acceptance tests in 501 seconds, zero skips. Five disposable behavioral reverts fail and pass after restoration; the package property separately detects removal of all 14 direct typed rethrow guards. Both PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc61bqZa and PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc61bqZi retain their runtime fix in 5b48dae, with added direct creator identity, misleading-guard, and packaged safe-cause controls in this continuation. All fast gates pass at unchanged thresholds; complete npm/Bun release and coverage gates require final-head CI at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/pull/51/checks under the original explicit host-duration exception. Threads remain open for orchestrator handling. No PM CLI/SDK defect encountered. Releasing this claim without closing the item."
